    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Expand and simplify $\\left(2x-\\dfrac{3}{x}\\right)^5$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$32x^5-240x^3+720x-\\dfrac{1080}{x}+\\dfrac{810}{x^3}-\\dfrac{243}{x^5}$",
      "worked": "Use the coefficients $1,5,10,10,5,1$ and take the second term as $-\\dfrac{3}{x}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\left(2x-\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^5&=\\sum_{k=0}^{5}\\binom{5}{k}(2x)^{5-k}\\left(-\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^k\\\\\n\\left(2x-\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^5&=32x^5-5(16)(3)x^3+10(8)(9)x-\\frac{10(4)(27)}{x}+\\frac{5(2)(81)}{x^3}-\\frac{243}{x^5}\\\\\n\\left(2x-\\frac{3}{x}\\right)^5&=32x^5-240x^3+720x-\\frac{1080}{x}+\\frac{810}{x^3}-\\frac{243}{x^5}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
